{:receipt :kotobase/materialized-view-gap
 :date "2026-08-17"

 :question
 "The cost model says routing served reads through materialised views is worth
  64x per query and moves the Neo4j-Aura crossover from 1M to 65M queries a
  month. I described that as designing which query shapes a view can answer.
  Is that actually the gap?"

 :answer "No. The design exists and is implemented. Nothing calls it."

 :what-already-exists
 {:capability "kotoba-lang/kotobase-projection -- `Portable, storage-neutral
               derived query artifacts for Kotobase`, extracted from
               kotobase-peer, with its own conformance tests."
  :view-building ["kotobase.projection/build-view"
                  "kotobase.projection/build-view-delta"
                  "kotobase.projection/compose-view-segments"
                  "kotobase.projection/build-datom-projection"]
  :view-reading ["kotobase.projection/range-query-plan"
                 "kotobase.projection/batch-point-query-plan"
                 "kotobase.projection/select-blocks"
                 "kotobase.projection/coalesce-block-ranges"
                 "kotobase.projection/build-bloom + bloom-might-contain?"
                 "kotobase.projection/object-range-get"]
  :incremental-maintenance ["kotobase.projection.datalog/maintain-query-delta"
                            "kotobase.projection.datalog/refresh-plan"
                            "kotobase.projection.datalog/affected-query-results"
                            "kotobase.projection.datalog/build-frontier-work-chain"
                            "kotobase.projection.datalog/frontier-step-plan"]
  :fold-time-views "kotobase-peer's `view-rows` / `put-views-block!` -- views
                    materialised at fold time, linked from chain state under
                    `views`, merged with unfolded novelty on read so a view is
                    always fresh."

  :the-admission-predicate-is-already-written
  "`kotobase.projection.datalog/positive-conjunctive-query?` -- no :rules, every
   :where clause a 3-element vector, every :find a variable. And
   `bounded-single-clause-query?` for the cheap path, whose own docstring draws
   the line I thought needed drawing: `Multi-clause queries need an
   arrangement/frontier loader and must not use this shortcut merely because
   their final result is small.`

   So `which query shapes can a materialised view answer` is not an open design
   question. It is a named, machine-checkable predicate in a shipped library."}

 :the-actual-gap
 {:measured "Read the production chain head for kotobase-protocols-v2 from R2
             (seq 972) and decoded its state node."
  :state-keys ["indexed" "novelty-back" "novelty-count" "novelty-front"]
  :views nil
  :reading "There is no `views` key at all. Not an empty map -- absent. Zero
            materialised views have ever been declared on the graph that every
            served surface reads."
  :classpath "protocols-worker's upstream-lock pins kotobase-projection
              (b35b0537) and its shadow-cljs.edn puts it on the source path, so
              the capability is COMPILED INTO the deployed bundle. No namespace
              in the worker's own source requires it."
  :so "The library is shipped, linked, and never invoked. The served path
       hydrates on every request instead, at ~1,364 CPU-ms and 85 R2 GETs."}

 :this-is-the-fourth-today
 "Capability built, tested, linked, never wired -- the same shape found three
  other times in one day: GraphSync (seven namespaces implementing
  /ipfs/graphsync/2.0.0, required by no deployed worker), the datalake engine
  (catalog, columnar, Parquet/Arrow readers, prefetch trampoline all landed;
  lake.kotobase.net still NXDOMAIN), and `:query-statistics` (implemented,
  unused for eleven days until 2026-08-13 wired it and took IC08 from 11.4x to
  1.85x). The pattern is worth naming on its own: this workspace's binding
  constraint is not capability, it is wiring."

 :correction
 "I wrote in the unit-economics artifact that item 1 was `make the MV path the
  default served route`, and then described it as a design project needing a
  decision about which queries a view can answer. Both halves were wrong in the
  same direction -- they placed work in the future that is already in the repo.
  The remaining work is: declare a view, call refresh-plan on write, and route
  the read. Smaller than described, and differently shaped."

 :what-is-genuinely-not-decided
 ["WHICH views to declare for this graph -- the predicate says what is
   admissible, not what is worth materialising. That needs the served query
   mix, which cannot be read from outside because the query surfaces require
   credentials."
  "Whether maintenance runs at fold time (kotobase-peer's existing `views`
   mechanism) or through kotobase-projection's differential path. Both exist;
   nothing chooses."
  "The 34 ms figure quoted for `the MV path` came from
   kotobase-peer.materialized-view's 2026-07-21 bench -- a pre-packed 100k-row
   view read by byte range. That is the same family as
   kotobase.projection/range-query-plan but it is not a measurement of this
   library on this graph, and it should not be quoted as one."]}
